<title>UK: European raw cotton market remains cautious.</title>
<headline>European raw cotton market remains cautious.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The caution inspired by the recent sharp increase on the New York cotton futures remained the dominant feature in Europe, industry sources said.</p>
<p>However, some enquiry was noted from mills with pressing requirements to cover, with the focus on Central Asian cotton.</p>
<p>Offers of Spanish and Greek cottons also attracted interest.</p>
</text>
